`expand_ranges(spec)` accepts a comma-separated string of either non-negative integers or inclusive ascending ranges such as `"2,5-7"`. It returns integers in textual expansion order, preserving duplicates. Whitespace around tokens and range endpoints is allowed. An empty or whitespace-only string returns `[]`. Empty tokens, negative numbers, descending ranges, extra hyphens, and non-numeric text raise `ValueError`. Non-string input raises `TypeError`.

